      "turn": 3,
      "action": {
        "type": "message",
        "message": "Could you explain the two Medicare paths again?"
      },
      "elapsed_seconds": 7.351,
      "reply": "Yes. There are two main paths: Original Medicare and Medicare Advantage. Original Medicare is Part A and Part B through the federal program; you can usually add a separate drug plan, and Medigap may help with out-of-pocket costs. Medicare Advantage is a private plan approved by Medicare that provides Parts A and B, and many plans include drug coverage. With either path, you still pay the Part B premium.",
